+/// Finds, read by read, what makes the preprocessor open a file no line marker names: an
+/// `#embed` directive or a `__has_embed` operator. Direct mode records a result against the
+/// line-marked files alone, so a translation unit holding either must be preprocessed every
+/// time; its preprocessed text then carries the embedded bytes (clang and gcc both expand them
+/// under `-E`), and the key with it.
+///
+/// The identifier `embed` anywhere counts, a variable named so too: that costs direct mode for
+/// the translation unit and nothing else. A line splice inside the word (`em\` newline `bed`)
+/// is missed, as [`TimeMacroFinder`] misses one inside `__TIME__`.
+#[derive(Debug, Default)]
+pub struct EmbedFinder {
+    /// The last `EMBED_WINDOW - 1` bytes read, for a match that straddles two reads.
+    tail: Vec<u8>,
+    found: bool,
+}
